  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#hasPrecedenceLevel">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">precedence level</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>binding_ratio | persuasive_obiter | constitutional_grand_chamber | authorial_transposition</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">binding_ratio | persuasive_obiter | constitutional_grand_chamber | authorial_transposition. The first three record how much interpretive weight a holding claims. The fourth marks a mapping the ontology designer has drawn across instruments or contexts, which is NOT a holding of the Court and must not be cited as one. This is an analytical metadata model adopted by MAILO, not a formal precedent hierarchy operated by the CJEU.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#LegalPrinciple"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <mailo:LiteratureSource rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#lit_Robaldo_L_Bartolini_C_Palmirani_M_et_al_2020_Fo">
    <rdfs:label>Robaldo, L., Bartolini, C., Palmirani, M., et al. (2020). Formalizing GDPR Provisions in Reified I/O Logic: The DAPRECO Knowledge Base. Journal of Logic, Language and Information.</rdfs:label>
    <dcterms:date>2020</dcterms:date>
    <dcterms:description>LegalRuleML + reified Input/Output logic + SPINDle defeasible reasoner. The canonical precedent for formal GDPR reasoning. Limitations addressed by MAILO: GDPR-only; no medical AI integration; no CJEU case-law layer; no runtime guardrail integration.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10849-019-09309-z"/>
    <mailo:relevanceScore rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</mailo:relevanceScore>
  </mailo:LiteratureSource>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#isActionable">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is actionable</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Explanation enables effective Art.22(3) remedies (C-203/22 P_203_001)</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">True if the explanation enables effective exercise of GDPR Art.22(3) remedies (C-203/22 P_203_001). Abstract mathematical formulas are insufficient.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#Explanation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <mailo:CrossFrameworkTension rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Tension_TSD_AIAct_Transparency">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">TSD Art.2 Trade Secret vs. AI Act Art.13 + GDPR Art.15(1)(h) — Core Transparency Tension</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">EHDS Art.52 is now encoded and provides the medical-domain resolution route for this tension: disclosure into a controlled environment under HDAB-imposed safeguards rather than to the requester. Added in v5.1.0.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Re-anchored in v5.1.0 to TSD Art.1(2)(b), which preserves rules requiring disclosure of trade secrets to administrative or judicial authorities. The Art.5 exceptions previously relied on concern freedom of expression and whistleblowing, not data-subject or regulatory disclosure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">TSD Art.2 protects model weights, training data schemas, and architecture as trade secrets. AI Act Art.13 requires deployers to receive sufficient information about high-risk AI system capabilities and limitations. C-203/22 §§59-62 sets the mandatory floor: controller cannot invoke TSD Art.2 to deny all causal explanation of an automated decision — disputed information must be produced to the competent supervisory authority or court for balance. AI Act Art.78 ensures national authority confidentiality but does not disapply Art.13 disclosure to deployers. TSD Art.5 is the only legislative bridge but its scope in the medical AI context remains unresolved pending a CJEU reference on Art.22 and clinical AI.</rdfs:comment>
    <mailo:conflictType rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#TradeSecretConflict"/>
    <mailo:conflictsWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#ExplainabilityObligation"/>
    <mailo:conflictsWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#TransparencyObligation"/>
    <mailo:hasResolutionStatus rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">partial</mailo:hasResolutionStatus>
    <mailo:involvesArticle rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#TSD_Art1_2"/>
    <mailo:involvesFramework rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct"/>
    <mailo:involvesFramework rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR"/>
    <mailo:involvesFramework rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#TSD"/>
  </mailo:CrossFrameworkTension>
