  <mailo:UPCCase rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#UPC_Dexcom_Abbott">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dexcom v. Abbott — Continuous Glucose Monitoring</rdfs:label>
    <dcterms:identifier>UPC_CFI_230/2023 (ACT_546446/2023)</dcterms:identifier>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">CORRECTED in v5.1.0. (1) The earlier record said the Paris LD revoked both EP 3 435 866 and EP 3 831 282. Only EP 866 was revoked in this decision; EP 282 was the subject of separate actions. (2) The recorded identifier ACT_583778/2023 is a different Paris action and does not correspond to the decision described; the correct reference is UPC_CFI_230/2023 (ACT_546446/2023). (3) decidedBy Munich LD is removed: Munich heard separate Dexcom actions, not this one. (4) involvesTechnology RiskScoringSystem is removed — a continuous glucose monitor is a sensing and measurement device, not a risk-scoring system. Whether any AI element is claimed has not been established, so no replacement technology is asserted.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inclusion basis (DirectSubjectMatter): Continuous glucose monitoring with algorithmic estimation.</rdfs:comment>
    <mailo:decidedBy>
      <mailo:UPCDivision rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#UPC_LD_Paris">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">UPC Local Division — Paris</rdfs:label>
      </mailo:UPCDivision>
    </mailo:decidedBy>
    <mailo:hasDefendant>
      <mailo:Company rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Abbott">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Abbott Laboratories</rdfs:label>
      </mailo:Company>
    </mailo:hasDefendant>
    <mailo:hasInclusionBasis rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#DirectSubjectMatter"/>
    <mailo:hasOutcome>Paris Local Division, 3 July 2024: on Dexcom's infringement action and Abbott's revocation counterclaim, EP 3 435 866 (remote monitoring of blood glucose) was revoked in its entirety for lack of inventive step, with effect across all UPC states. The patent had previously been maintained by the EPO in opposition on substantially the same grounds and prior art, making this a documented EPO-UPC divergence. The parties settled all patent disputes worldwide on 23 December 2024.</mailo:hasOutcome>
    <mailo:hasPlaintiff>
      <mailo:Company rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Dexcom">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dexcom Inc.</rdfs:label>
      </mailo:Company>
    </mailo:hasPlaintiff>
    <mailo:hasStatus>Settled globally 23 December 2024; all pending cases dismissed (verified 2026-09-10)</mailo:hasStatus>
  </mailo:UPCCase>
