    <rdfs:comment>Cites another CJEU case (alias)</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#CJEUCase"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#CJEUCase"/>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#oversightIsSubstantive">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">oversight is substantive</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>True = genuine review; false = rubber-stamping (C-634/21 P_634_002)</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">True if the human reviewer exercised independent judgment; false if the review was a mere formality (rubber-stamping). C-634/21 P_634_002 requires true.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#HumanOversightRecord"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#hasIndividualNonAutomatedReview">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has individual non-automated review</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>True = individual non-automated review before any measure (C-817/19 P_817_001)</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">True if every positive automated match is subject to individual non-automated human review before any measure is taken. C-817/19 P_817_001 constitutional minimum.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AutomatedDecisionSystem"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#hasVersion">
    <rdfs:comment>Regulation has a temporal applicability version</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#EURegulation"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#RegulationVersion"/>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#hasPrinciple">
    <rdfs:comment>Establishes a legal principle (alias)</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#CJEUCase"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#LegalPrinciple"/>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <mailo:EPOProceding rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#EPO_G0001_19">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EPO G 0001/19 — Patentability of Computer-Implemented Simulations</rdfs:label>
    <dcterms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2021-03-10</dcterms:date>
    <dcterms:identifier>G 0001/19</dcterms:identifier>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">CORRECTED in v5.1.0. The earlier record stated that 'computer-implemented simulation of a technical process is not excluded from patentability (Art.52(2))'. Two errors. First, the Enlarged Board held that whether the SIMULATED system or process is technical is NOT decisive, so framing the holding around simulation of a technical process inverts the point. Second, the decision is an INVENTIVE STEP ruling under the COMVIK approach, not an Art.52(2) exclusion ruling: the eligibility hurdle is passed by any computer implementation and the analysis happens at Art.56. interpretesArticle is corrected from Art.52 to Art.56. Note this is the third instance of the same pattern in MAILO's EPO material — T 0161/18 and T 1191/19 were both attributed to Art.52 when they turn on Arts.83 and 56.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inclusion basis (TransposedPrinciple): Computer-implemented simulation generally. MAILO applies the technical-character reasoning to clinical simulation; the Enlarged Board did not rule on medical AI.</rdfs:comment>
    <mailo:decidedBy>
      <mailo:Court rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#EPO_EnlargedBoA">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EPO Enlarged Board of Appeal</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Ensures uniform application of the EPC and decides points of law referred to it. Declared in v5.1.0: it was already in use as the decidedBy value of G 1/19 but had never been typed.</rdfs:comment>
      </mailo:Court>
    </mailo:decidedBy>
    <mailo:hasInclusionBasis rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#TransposedPrinciple"/>
    <mailo:hasOutcome>Enlarged Board of Appeal, 10 March 2021 (application EP03793825.5, simulation of pedestrian crowd movement through a building). The COMVIK approach of T 641/00 applies to computer-implemented simulations, which are assessed by the same criteria as any other computer-implemented invention. A technical effect going beyond the normal electrical interactions within the computer — a further technical effect — is required to contribute to inventive step, and any further technical use of the simulation output must be at least implied by the claim. Question 2B was answered in the negative: it is NEITHER SUFFICIENT NOR NECESSARY that the simulation is based on technical principles underlying the simulated system.</mailo:hasOutcome>
    <mailo:interpretesArticle rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#EPC_Art56"/>
  </mailo:EPOProceding>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#hasTemporalLimitation">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has temporal limitation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Tri-level proportionality (c): temporal limitation or review schedule</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Tri-level proportionality test (c): temporal limitation or mandatory periodic review. C-817/19 P_817_003.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AutomatedDecisionSystem"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <mailo:LiteratureSource rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#lit_DAOnt_A_Formal_Ontology_for_EU_Data_Act_Compliance_2024_2">
    <rdfs:label>DAOnt: A Formal Ontology for EU Data Act Compliance. (2024/2026). arXiv:2604.16386.</rdfs:label>
    <dcterms:date>2024</dcterms:date>
    <dcterms:description>Reuses LKIF-Core + ODRL + DPV. Single-framework analogue of MAILO's multi-framework target.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:source rdf:resource="https://arxiv.org/html/2604.16386"/>
    <mailo:relevanceScore rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</mailo:relevanceScore>
  </mailo:LiteratureSource>
