  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#involvesArticle">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">involves article</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a CrossFrameworkTension to a provision it turns on. Added in v5.1.0: tensions cited annexes in prose that the ontology did not encode, so nothing connected the claim to the source.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <mailo:UPCCase rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#UPC_Sanofi_Amgen">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sanofi &amp; Regeneron v. Amgen — PCSK9 Medical Use</rdfs:label>
    <dcterms:identifier>UPC_CFI_505/2024</dcterms:identifier>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inclusion basis (DirectSubjectMatter): Antibody claims; biologic rather than AI, retained for claim-scope reasoning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">SCOPE CORRECTION and UNVERIFIED (v5.1.0). The instance was declared DirectSubjectMatter while its own note concedes the case is 'biologic rather than AI' — an internal contradiction. PCSK9 antibody claims involve no AI, so the basis is moved to DomainContext. The substantive assertions — a Dusseldorf LD finding of validity without infringement, a 'dual-element test', Court of Appeal restoration of EP'797 after Munich CD revocation, and an EPO Board hearing in April 2026 — are separately checkable and none has been verified. The status date has now passed. This is also the only UPC instance recording neither plaintiff nor defendant. Do not cite until checked.</rdfs:comment>
    <mailo:decidedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#UPC_LD_Dusseldorf"/>
    <mailo:hasInclusionBasis rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#DomainContext"/>
    <mailo:hasOutcome rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Düsseldorf LD: patent valid, no infringement (dual-element test established). CoA: EP'797 restored after Munich CD revocation. EPO-UPC divergence on inventive step.</mailo:hasOutcome>
    <mailo:hasStatus rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Active — EPO BoA hearing scheduled 2026-04</mailo:hasStatus>
  </mailo:UPCCase>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#hasHighRiskRoute">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has high-risk route</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Records how a system qualifies as high-risk. Determines the availability of the Art.86 right to explanation and the Art.26(11) notification duty, neither of which reaches Annex I systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AutomatedDecisionSystem"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#HighRiskRoute"/>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#chamberType">
    <rdfs:comment>Grand Chamber, Chamber, etc.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#producesSignificantImpact">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">produces significant impact</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>True if outputs have legal/similarly significant effects on individuals</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">True if the system's outputs have legal or similarly significant effects on individuals (C-634/21 P_634_001). Triggers full Art.22 obligation chain.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AutomatedDecisionSystem"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#hasPendingAmendment">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has pending amendment</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a LegalArticle whose numbering or content is currently in force to a proposed amendment that has not been adopted. Asserting this property makes no claim that the amendment will pass.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#LegalArticle"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#PendingAmendment"/>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#ecliIdentifier">
    <rdfs:comment>ECLI case identifier</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <mailo:CJEUCase rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#C_511_18">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">C-511/18 La Quadrature du Net</rdfs:label>
    <dcterms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2020-10-06</dcterms:date>
    <dcterms:identifier>C-511/18</dcterms:identifier>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inclusion basis (TransposedPrinciple): Bulk data retention. Retained for the proportionality line feeding C-817/19.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">MISSING METADATA (v5.1.0): no ECLI recorded. Not supplied here because it was not verified against a primary source in this pass, and asserting an identifier from memory is the error class that produced the original C-203/22 defect. Add after checking EUR-Lex.</rdfs:comment>
    <mailo:citesPrecedent>
      <mailo:CJEUCase rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#C_201_14">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">C-201/14 Bara</rdfs:label>
        <dcterms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2015-10-01</dcterms:date>
        <dcterms:identifier>C-201/14</dcterms:identifier>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inclusion basis (TransposedPrinciple): Health data transferred between public bodies without information; earliest link in the retained chain.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">MISSING METADATA (v5.1.0): no ECLI recorded. Not supplied here because it was not verified against a primary source in this pass, and asserting an identifier from memory is the error class that produced the original C-203/22 defect. Add after checking EUR-Lex.</rdfs:comment>
        <mailo:establishesPrinciple rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#P_Bara_001"/>
        <mailo:hasInclusionBasis rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#TransposedPrinciple"/>
        <mailo:hasStatus rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Final</mailo:hasStatus>
      </mailo:CJEUCase>
    </mailo:citesPrecedent>
    <mailo:hasInclusionBasis rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#TransposedPrinciple"/>
    <mailo:hasStatus rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Final</mailo:hasStatus>
  </mailo:CJEUCase>
  <mailo:ComplianceRisk rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Risk_DataActIoT">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Data Act Art.3/5 IoT Data Sharing Obligation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Medical device manufacturers must share IoT-generated health data with users/third parties. Conflicts with trade secret protection (Art.15) and competitive AI training data strategies.</rdfs:comment>
    <mailo:riskLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MEDIUM</mailo:riskLevel>
  </mailo:ComplianceRisk>
  <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#PLD_Art9">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PLD Art.9 — Disclosure Obligations (Evidence Facilitation)</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Courts may order defendants to disclose evidence about high-risk AI systems; creates procedural discovery mechanism absent in AILD.</rdfs:comment>
  </mailo:LegalArticle>
  <mailo:LegislativeAmendment rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Amend_AIAct_v3a_Omnibus_AnnexIII_Standalone">
    <rdfs:label>Activation event: high_risk_annex_iii_omnibus</rdfs:label>
    <mailo:amendmentDescription>Omnibus VII provisional agreement — Annex III standalone systems: 2027-12-02. Conditional on harmonised standards availability (Article 6(2) revised).</mailo:amendmentDescription>
    <mailo:versionStartDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2027-12-02</mailo:versionStartDate>
  </mailo:LegislativeAmendment>
  <mailo:CJEUCase rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#C_817_19">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">C-817/19 Ligue des droits humains v. Conseil des ministres</rdfs:label>
    <dcterms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2022-06-21</dcterms:date>
    <dcterms:identifier>C-817/19</dcterms:identifier>
    <dcterms:identifier>ECLI:EU:C:2022:491</dcterms:identifier>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A citesPrecedent link to C-634/21 (SCHUFA) was removed in v5.2.0 as temporally impossible: this judgment is of 21 June 2022 and SCHUFA was decided on 7 December 2023. The influence runs the other way.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inclusion basis (TransposedPrinciple): PNR / counter-terrorism. MAILO transposes the Grand Chamber's automated-decision safeguards to medical AI by structural analogy.</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:notation>ECLI:EU:C:2022:491</skos:notation>
    <mailo:citesPrecedent rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#C_511_18"/>
    <mailo:decidedBy>
      <mailo:Court rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#CJEU_GrandChamber">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CJEU Grand Chamber</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Highest formation of CJEU; judgments carry maximum precedential weight.</rdfs:comment>
      </mailo:Court>
    </mailo:decidedBy>
    <mailo:establishesPrinciple>
      <mailo:RatioDecidendi rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#P_817_001">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">P-817/19-001: Mandatory Non-Automated Individual Review</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Any positive match from automated PNR analysis must be subject to individual non-automated review before any measure is taken. Establishes constitutional minimum for meaningful human intervention.</rdfs:comment>
        <mailo:appliesTo rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AutomatedDecisionSystem"/>
        <mailo:appliesTo rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#MedicalAISystem"/>
        <mailo:hasEncodingBasis rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#CourtHolding"/>
        <mailo:hasPrecedenceLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">constitutional_grand_chamber</mailo:hasPrecedenceLevel>
        <mailo:triggersObligation rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#HumanOversightObligation"/>
      </mailo:RatioDecidendi>
    </mailo:establishesPrinciple>
    <mailo:establishesPrinciple>
      <mailo:RatioDecidendi rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#P_817_002">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">P-817/19-002: Black-Box ML Prohibition</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Non-transparent, self-learning ML risk assessment systems may not be used for decisions with significant impact. Pre-determined criteria and regular review are required.</rdfs:comment>
        <mailo:appliesTo rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#BlackBoxMLSystem"/>
        <mailo:appliesTo rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#MedicalAISystem"/>
        <mailo:hasEncodingBasis rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#CourtHolding"/>
        <mailo:hasPrecedenceLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">constitutional_grand_chamber</mailo:hasPrecedenceLevel>
        <mailo:triggersObligation rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#ExplainabilityObligation"/>
        <mailo:triggersObligation rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#TransparencyObligation"/>
      </mailo:RatioDecidendi>
    </mailo:establishesPrinciple>
    <mailo:establishesPrinciple>
      <mailo:RatioDecidendi rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#P_817_003">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">P-817/19-003: Strict Necessity Tri-Level Proportionality Test</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Large-scale automated processing must satisfy: (a) targeted scope (C-817/19 paras 167-168, 184, 191), (b) purpose limitation (para 191), (c) temporal limitation (paras 255-256, 262). The Court upheld the PNR Directive subject to Charter-conforming restrictive interpretation; non-conformity at a limb is flagged for review and does not entail invalidity.</rdfs:comment>
        <mailo:appliesTo rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AutomatedDecisionSystem"/>
        <mailo:hasEncodingBasis rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#CourtHolding"/>
        <mailo:hasPrecedenceLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">constitutional_grand_chamber</mailo:hasPrecedenceLevel>
      </mailo:RatioDecidendi>
    </mailo:establishesPrinciple>
    <mailo:establishesPrinciple>
      <mailo:RatioDecidendi rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#P_817_004">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">P-817/19-004: Non-Discrimination — Health Status Excluded</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Pre-determined assessment criteria may in no circumstances be based on health (PNR Directive Art.6(4); C-817/19 paras 105, 196-197) — a categorical prohibition, not a special-category rule curable by a GDPR Art.9(2) basis. MAILO transposes this to medical AI as a bar on using health condition as a discriminatory classification or risk-scoring criterion, which is narrower than any processing of health data.</rdfs:comment>
        <mailo:appliesTo rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#GenomicDiagnosticAI"/>
        <mailo:appliesTo rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#MedicalAISystem"/>
        <mailo:hasEncodingBasis rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#CourtHolding"/>
        <mailo:hasPrecedenceLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">constitutional_grand_chamber</mailo:hasPrecedenceLevel>
      </mailo:RatioDecidendi>
    </mailo:establishesPrinciple>
    <mailo:establishesPrinciple>
      <mailo:ObiterDictum rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#P_817_005">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">P-817/19-005: Independent Prior Review (and MAILO's DPIA bridge)</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">C-817/19 paras 222-227 (PNR Directive Art.12(3)(b)): disclosure after the initial period requires prior review by a court or independent administrative authority, which must be objective, impartial, free from external influence, and distinct from the requesting authority or the PIU. The Court said nothing about GDPR Art.35 or DPIAs; the link from independent prior review to a DPIA obligation for medical AI is an authorial cross-instrument interpretation by the ontology designer, not a holding. The DPIA requirement stands on GDPR Art.35 alone.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Encoding basis (DesignerTransposition): C-817/19 paras 222-227 concern prior review of PNR disclosure requests. The bridge to a GDPR Art.35 DPIA duty is the designer's; the DPIA constraint stands on Art.35 alone.</rdfs:comment>
        <mailo:hasEncodingBasis rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#DesignerTransposition"/>
        <mailo:hasPrecedenceLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">authorial_transposition</mailo:hasPrecedenceLevel>
        <mailo:triggersObligation rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#DPIAObligation"/>
      </mailo:ObiterDictum>
    </mailo:establishesPrinciple>
    <mailo:hasInclusionBasis rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#TransposedPrinciple"/>
    <mailo:hasOutcome rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PNR Directive valid only with strict necessity; black-box ML systems prohibited; mandatory non-automated individual review; health status excluded from automated criteria.</mailo:hasOutcome>
    <mailo:hasStatus rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Final — Grand Chamber binding precedent</mailo:hasStatus>
    <mailo:interpretesArticle>
      <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Charter_Art7">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EU Charter Art.7 — Respect for private and family life</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Everyone has the right to respect for his or her private and family life, home and communications. Together with Art.8 the constitutional basis against which the Court assessed the PNR Directive in C-817/19 and the retention regimes in C-511/18.</rdfs:comment>
      </mailo:LegalArticle>
    </mailo:interpretesArticle>
    <mailo:interpretesArticle>
      <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Charter_Art8">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EU Charter Art.8 — Protection of personal data</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Everyone has the right to the protection of personal data concerning him or her; such data must be processed fairly, for specified purposes and on a legitimate basis laid down by law; everyone has the right of access to data collected concerning them and the right to have it rectified; and compliance is subject to control by an independent authority. Art.8(2) is the Charter root of the GDPR Art.15 access right that C-203/22 and C-307/22 interpret; Art.8(3) is the independent-supervision requirement echoed in C-817/19 paras 222-227.</rdfs:comment>
      </mailo:LegalArticle>
    </mailo:interpretesArticle>
    <mailo:involvesTechnology rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AutomatedDecisionSystem"/>
    <mailo:involvesTechnology rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#BlackBoxMLSystem"/>
  </mailo:CJEUCase>
  <mailo:RegulationVersion rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_v4_FRIA_PublicBodies">
    <rdfs:label>FRIA obligation for public-body deployers applies (Art.27)</rdfs:label>
    <mailo:applicablePhase>fria_public_bodies</mailo:applicablePhase>
    <mailo:isCurrentVersion rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">false</mailo:isCurrentVersion>
    <mailo:triggeredBy>
      <mailo:LegislativeAmendment rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Amend_AIAct_v4_FRIA_PublicBodies">
        <rdfs:label>Activation event: fria_public_bodies</rdfs:label>
        <mailo:amendmentDescription>36-month anniversary — Fundamental Rights Impact Assessment mandatory for public-body deployers of high-risk AI systems</mailo:amendmentDescription>
        <mailo:versionStartDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2027-08-02</mailo:versionStartDate>
      </mailo:LegislativeAmendment>
    </mailo:triggeredBy>
    <mailo:versionOf>
      <mailo:EURegulation rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_2024_1689">
        <rdfs:label>AI Act 2024/1689</rdfs:label>
        <mailo:celex>32024R1689</mailo:celex>
        <mailo:hasVersion rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_v1_ProhibitedPractices"/>
        <mailo:hasVersion rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_v2_GPAIModelObligations"/>
        <mailo:hasVersion rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_v3_OriginalHighRisk"/>
        <mailo:hasVersion rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_v3a_Omnibus_AnnexIII_Standalone"/>
        <mailo:hasVersion rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_v3b_Omnibus_AnnexI_SaMD"/>
        <mailo:hasVersion rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_v4_FRIA_PublicBodies"/>
      </mailo:EURegulation>
    </mailo:versionOf>
    <mailo:versionStartDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2027-08-02</mailo:versionStartDate>
  </mailo:RegulationVersion>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#EUDirective">
    <rdfs:label>EUDirective</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EU Directive</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>EU Directive (requires transposition)</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#LegalInstrument"/>
  </owl:Class>
  <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_Art35">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">GDPR Article 35</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Data Protection Impact Assessment (DPIA).</rdfs:comment>
  </mailo:LegalArticle>
  <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#TSD_Art3">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">TSD Art.3 — Lawful acquisition, use and disclosure</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Acquisition is lawful where obtained by independent discovery or creation, or by observation, study, disassembly or testing of a product or object that has been made available to the public or is lawfully in the possession of the acquirer who is free of any legally valid duty to limit the acquisition — that is, REVERSE ENGINEERING is lawful acquisition unless contractually excluded. Directly relevant to medical AI: analysing a deployed model's behaviour through observation and testing is not an unlawful acquisition of the trade secrets it embodies, which bears on both explainability research and the practical reach of secrecy over deployed systems. Added in v5.1.0.</rdfs:comment>
  </mailo:LegalArticle>
  <mailo:ComplianceRisk rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Risk_BlackBox">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Black-Box ML System (C-817/19 Prohibition)</rdfs:label>
    <mailo:mitigatedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#ExplainabilityObligation"/>
    <mailo:mitigatedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#TransparencyObligation"/>
    <mailo:riskLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">HIGH</mailo:riskLevel>
  </mailo:ComplianceRisk>
  <mailo:RatioDecidendi rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#P_634_004">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">P-634/21-004: Art.22 = Prohibition Rule</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Art.22(1) is a prohibition rule, not merely a right to object. Exceptions in Art.22(2) are exhaustive; safeguards in Art.22(3) are mandatory when an exception applies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Encoding basis (DesignerOperationalisation): The characterisation of Art.22(1) as a prohibition rather than a right to be invoked is not anchored to its own paragraphs and remains contested in the literature. Recorded as the designer's reading pending verification.</rdfs:comment>
    <mailo:hasEncodingBasis>
      <mailo:EncodingBasis rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#DesignerOperationalisation">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Designer operationalisation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The court's test is open-textured and the constraint encodes a proxy for it. The paragraphs are correct; the operative predicate is MAILO's. Example: C-634/21 states a determining-role test; the substantive-oversight predicate is a proxy for it.</rdfs:comment>
      </mailo:EncodingBasis>
    </mailo:hasEncodingBasis>
    <mailo:hasPrecedenceLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">persuasive_obiter</mailo:hasPrecedenceLevel>
  </mailo:RatioDecidendi>
  <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_Art22_2">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">GDPR Art.22(2) — Derogations</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Art.22(1) does not apply where the decision is (a) necessary for entering into or performance of a contract between data subject and controller, (b) authorised by Union or Member State law to which the controller is subject and which lays down suitable measures to safeguard rights, freedoms and legitimate interests, or (c) based on the data subject's explicit consent.</rdfs:comment>
  </mailo:LegalArticle>
  <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#MDR_AnnexVIII_Rule11">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">MDR Annex VIII Rule 11 — Classification of software</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Software intended to provide information used to take decisions with diagnosis or therapeutic purposes is Class IIa, rising to Class III where such decisions may cause death or an irreversible deterioration of health, and to Class IIb where they may cause a serious deterioration or surgical intervention. Software intended to monitor physiological processes is Class IIa, or IIb where monitoring vital parameters whose variation could result in immediate danger. All other software is Class I.

This is the linchpin connecting MDR to the AI Act and was absent from MAILO. Rule 11 places most diagnostic and decision-support software at Class IIa or above, which requires notified-body conformity assessment, which in turn makes the system high-risk under AI Act Art.6(1) by the ANNEX I route — and therefore outside the Art.86 right to explanation. The dual-track burden and the Art.86 exclusion both follow from this classification rule. Added in v5.1.0.</rdfs:comment>
    <mailo:triggersRoute>
      <mailo:HighRiskRoute rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#AnnexIRoute">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Annex I route (Art.6(1)) — product or safety component</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The system is a product, or a safety component of a product, covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I and required to undergo third-party conformity assessment. MDR and IVDR are in Annex I Section A, so Class IIa, IIb and III medical devices incorporating AI take this route automatically. Art.86 and Art.26(11), both scoped to Annex III, DO NOT APPLY. Obligations for this route apply from 2 August 2028.</rdfs:comment>
      </mailo:HighRiskRoute>
    </mailo:triggersRoute>
  </mailo:LegalArticle>
  <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#MDR_AnnexI">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">MDR Annex I — General safety and performance requirements</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The GSPRs a device must meet. Chapter II section 17 governs electronic programmable systems and software: devices incorporating such systems shall be designed to ensure repeatability, reliability and performance in line with their intended use, software shall be developed and manufactured in accordance with the state of the art taking account of the development lifecycle, risk management including information security, verification and validation. The provision against which AI-specific validation expectations are read. Added in v5.1.0.</rdfs:comment>
  </mailo:LegalArticle>
  <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_Art14">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">AI Act Art.14 — Human oversight</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">High-risk AI systems shall be designed and developed so that they can be effectively overseen by natural persons during use, including through appropriate human-machine interface tools. Oversight measures aim to prevent or minimise risks to health, safety or fundamental rights, and must enable the person to understand capacities and limitations, remain aware of automation bias, correctly interpret output, disregard or override it, and intervene or stop the system. The complementedBy link to GDPR Art.22(3) should be read subject to the note on that article: the Art.22(3) safeguards attach only to Art.22(2)(a) and (c), so oversight under Art.14 and the data-protection safeguards do not automatically coincide.</rdfs:comment>
    <mailo:complementedBy>
      <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_Art22_3">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">GDPR Art.22(3) — Safeguards, applying only to points (a) and (c) of Art.22(2)</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">In the cases referred to in POINTS (a) AND (c) of Art.22(2), the controller shall implement suitable measures to safeguard the data subject's rights, freedoms and legitimate interests, at least the right to obtain human intervention on the controller's part, to express his or her point of view and to contest the decision. CORRECTED in v5.1.0: the earlier text said these safeguards apply whenever an exception applies. They do NOT attach to point (b): where the basis is Union or Member State law, that law must itself lay down suitable measures. The distinction is material for medical AI operating on a national legal basis, where the Art.22(3) triad cannot simply be assumed.</rdfs:comment>
        <mailo:grantsRight rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#Right_Contest"/>
        <mailo:grantsRight rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#Right_ExpressViews"/>
        <mailo:grantsRight rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#Right_HumanIntervention"/>
      </mailo:LegalArticle>
    </mailo:complementedBy>
  </mailo:LegalArticle>
  <mailo:RegulationVersion rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_v2_OmnibusProposed_Art22">
    <rdfs:label>GDPR Art.22 Omnibus-proposed version — permission list framing (PROSPECTIVE, NOT ADOPTED)</rdfs:label>
    <mailo:applicablePhase>art22_omnibus_proposed_NOT_ADOPTED</mailo:applicablePhase>
    <mailo:isCurrentVersion rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">false</mailo:isCurrentVersion>
    <mailo:triggeredBy>
      <mailo:LegislativeAmendment rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#OmnibusGDPR_Art22_Proposal_20251119">
        <rdfs:label>Digital Omnibus Regulation — GDPR Art.22 Reframing Proposal (NOT YET ADOPTED)</rdfs:label>
        <mailo:amendmentDescription>Commission proposal (2025-11-19) to replace GDPR Art.22(1)-(2) prohibition structure with an exhaustive positive permission list for solely automated decision-making. EDPB-EDPS Joint Opinion 2/2026 (2026-02-11) strongly opposes the reframing, citing CJEU confirmation of Art.22 as a prohibition in principle (C-634/21, C-817/19). Status: UNADOPTED — in trilogue negotiation as of 2026-05-10. MAILO SHACL shapes remain grounded in current prohibition structure. If adopted, NodeShapes C634_Art22ProhibitionShape and related shapes require reformulation to encode positive permission conditions rather than absence of exception.</mailo:amendmentDescription>
        <mailo:versionStartDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-11-19</mailo:versionStartDate>
      </mailo:LegislativeAmendment>
    </mailo:triggeredBy>
    <mailo:versionOf>
      <mailo:EURegulation rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_2016_679">
        <rdfs:label>GDPR 2016/679</rdfs:label>
        <mailo:celex>32016R0679</mailo:celex>
        <mailo:hasVersion rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_v1_FullyApplicable"/>
        <mailo:hasVersion rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_v2_OmnibusProposed_Art22"/>
      </mailo:EURegulation>
    </mailo:versionOf>
  </mailo:RegulationVersion>
  <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#TSD_Art2">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">TSD Article 2 — Definition of Trade Secret</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Three-part cumulative test: information must be (1) secret (not generally known or readily accessible), (2) have commercial value because it is secret, and (3) be subject to reasonable steps to keep it secret. All three must hold for ML model weights or training data to qualify.</rdfs:comment>
  </mailo:LegalArticle>
  <mailo:ComplianceRisk rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Risk_SolelyTest">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">GDPR Art.22 'Solely' Test Failure (Rubber-Stamping)</rdfs:label>
    <mailo:mitigatedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#HumanOversightObligation"/>
    <mailo:riskLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CRITICAL</mailo:riskLevel>
  </mailo:ComplianceRisk>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#LegalEntity">
    <rdfs:label>LegalEntity</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Legal Entity</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Any natural or legal person with legal standing</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#GenomicDiagnosticAI">
    <rdfs:label>GenomicDiagnosticAI</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genomic Diagnostic AI</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>AI system for genomic/genetic diagnostics</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#MedicalAISystem"/>
    <mailo:hasRisk>
      <mailo:ComplianceRisk rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Risk_EHDSOptOut">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EHDS Art.35 Opt-Out Erodes Training Dataset</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Widespread exercise of opt-out rights under EHDS Art.35 may substantially reduce available health data for AI training, creating representativeness risk under AI Act Art.10.</rdfs:comment>
        <mailo:riskLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MEDIUM</mailo:riskLevel>
      </mailo:ComplianceRisk>
    </mailo:hasRisk>
    <mailo:hasRisk>
      <mailo:ComplianceRisk rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Risk_NPE_Revocation">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">NPE-Initiated Revocation Attack</rdfs:label>
        <mailo:riskLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MEDIUM</mailo:riskLevel>
      </mailo:ComplianceRisk>
    </mailo:hasRisk>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Company">
    <rdfs:label>Company</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Company</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>A corporate entity</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#LegalEntity"/>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#CJEUCase">
    <rdfs:label>CJEUCase</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CJEU Case</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Judgment of the Court of Justice of the EU</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Preliminary ruling or direct action before the Court of Justice of the EU.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#Case"/>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#LegalArticle">
    <rdfs:label>LegalArticle</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Legal Article</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>A specific provision within a legal instrument</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A specific provision within a legal instrument.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#LegalExpression"/>
  </owl:Class>
  <mailo:ComplianceRisk rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Risk_InsufficientDisclosure">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Insufficient Training Data Disclosure (EPO T0161/18)</rdfs:label>
    <mailo:mitigatedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#DisclosureObligation"/>
    <mailo:riskLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">HIGH</mailo:riskLevel>
  </mailo:ComplianceRisk>
  <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#DGA_Art3">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">DGA Art.3 — Categories of protected public sector data eligible for re-use</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Opens Chapter II (Arts 3-9) by fixing the categories of protected data held by public sector bodies whose re-use the Regulation conditions, including data subject to statistical or commercial confidentiality and personal data. The substantive re-use conditions, including anonymisation and the secure processing environment, are in Art.5. Applies to AI training use cases at hospitals and research institutes. Corrected in v5.1.0 Round 5: previously recorded as Art.2, the Definitions article.</rdfs:comment>
  </mailo:LegalArticle>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#HumanOversightObligation">
    <rdfs:label>HumanOversightObligation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Human Oversight Obligation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Obligation to ensure substantive human review</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/airo#HumanOversight"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#ComplianceObligation"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/dpv#HumanInvolvement"/>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#AutomatedDecisionSystem">
    <rdfs:label>AutomatedDecisionSystem</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Automated Decision System</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>System processing personal data without meaningful human review</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A system that processes personal data to produce outputs affecting individuals without meaningful human review.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Corrected in v5.1.0: this class was declared rdfs:subClassOf mailo:MedicalAISystem, which entailed that every automated decision system is a medical AI system. The credit-scoring systems in C-634/21 and C-203/22 are counter-examples in MAILO's own graph. The relation runs the other way: a medical AI system producing decisions about individuals IS an automated decision system, which is why MedicalAISystem is now the subclass.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/dpv#DataProcessing"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#Technology"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/dpv#AutomatedDecisionMaking"/>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#ObiterDictum">
    <rdfs:label>ObiterDictum</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Obiter Dictum</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Persuasive (non-binding) judicial observation</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Persuasive (non-binding) judicial observation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#LegalPrinciple"/>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#EPOProceding">
    <rdfs:label>EPOProceding</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EPO Proceeding</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>EPO opposition, appeal, or examination</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Opposition, appeal, or examination proceeding before the EPO.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#Case"/>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#ExplainabilityObligation">
    <rdfs:label>ExplainabilityObligation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Explainability Obligation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Obligation to provide actionable explanations</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/dpv#ExplainabilityObligation"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#ComplianceObligation"/>
  </owl:Class>
  <mailo:RegulationVersion rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_v1_FullyApplicable">
    <rdfs:label>GDPR fully applicable — all provisions in force</rdfs:label>
    <mailo:applicablePhase>fully_applicable</mailo:applicablePhase>
    <mailo:isCurrentVersion rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</mailo:isCurrentVersion>
    <mailo:versionOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_2016_679"/>
    <mailo:versionStartDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2018-05-25</mailo:versionStartDate>
  </mailo:RegulationVersion>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#BlackBoxMLSystem">
    <rdfs:label>BlackBoxMLSystem</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Black-Box ML System</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Non-transparent self-learning ML system (C-817/19 prohibition)</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A non-transparent, self-learning system whose decision logic cannot be explained. Prohibited under C-817/19 for decisions with significant impact.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Corrected in v5.1.0: previously declared a subclass of MedicalAISystem. Opacity is a property of a system's decision logic, not of its clinical application; the PNR system in C-817/19 was not medical.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/airo#OpaqueSystem"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AutomatedDecisionSystem"/>
  </owl:Class>
  <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#EHDS_Art23">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EHDS Art.23 — MyHealth@EU (cross-border infrastructure for PRIMARY use)</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The cross-border infrastructure for primary use, to be distinguished from HealthData@EU at Art.75, which serves secondary use. Added in v5.1.0 because the two were previously conflatable: the superseded Art.50 entry described HealthData@EU using proposal numbering with no primary-use counterpart recorded.</rdfs:comment>
  </mailo:LegalArticle>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#MedicalImagingAI">
    <rdfs:label>MedicalImagingAI</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Medical Imaging AI</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>AI system for medical image analysis</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#MedicalAISystem"/>
    <mailo:hasRisk rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#Risk_DataActIoT"/>
    <mailo:hasRisk>
      <mailo:ComplianceRisk rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Risk_EPOUPC_Divergence">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EPO-UPC Divergent Validity Rulings (Opt-Out Strategy)</rdfs:label>
        <mailo:riskLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">HIGH</mailo:riskLevel>
      </mailo:ComplianceRisk>
    </mailo:hasRisk>
  </owl:Class>
  <mailo:PendingAmendment rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#DigitalOmnibus_DataAct_ChapterV">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Digital Omnibus — proposed consolidation of Data Act Chapter V into a new Art.15a</rdfs:label>
    <mailo:amendmentProcedureRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2025/0360(COD)</mailo:amendmentProcedureRef>
    <mailo:amendmentProposalRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">COM(2025) 837 final</mailo:amendmentProposalRef>
    <mailo:legislativeStatus rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">council_position</mailo:legislativeStatus>
    <mailo:proposedEffect rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Deletes Data Act Arts 14 and 15 and consolidates the business-to-government regime into a new Art.15a, narrowing the trigger from 'exceptional need' to public emergencies only. Not adopted as at the verification date: the AI limb of the Digital Omnibus was severed and adopted separately as Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, while the data limb remains in negotiation. MAILO therefore continues to encode the numbering of Regulation (EU) 2023/2854 as published.</mailo:proposedEffect>
    <mailo:proposedRenumberingTo rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Data Act Art.15a</mailo:proposedRenumberingTo>
    <mailo:statusVerifiedAsAt rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-05</mailo:statusVerifiedAsAt>
  </mailo:PendingAmendment>
  <mailo:ComplianceRisk rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Risk_PLDStrictLiability">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PLD 2024 Strict Liability for AI-SaMD</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Medical AI systems qualifying as 'defective products' under PLD Art.4 expose manufacturers to strict liability without fault. Presumptions in Art.10 and Art.11 shift burden to defendants.</rdfs:comment>
    <mailo:mitigatedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#HumanOversightObligation"/>
    <mailo:mitigatedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#TransparencyObligation"/>
    <mailo:riskLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">HIGH</mailo:riskLevel>
  </mailo:ComplianceRisk>
  <mailo:RegulationVersion rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_v1_ProhibitedPractices">
    <rdfs:label>Prohibited AI practices (Art.5) and general provisions in force</rdfs:label>
    <mailo:applicablePhase>prohibited_practices_and_general</mailo:applicablePhase>
    <mailo:isCurrentVersion rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">false</mailo:isCurrentVersion>
    <mailo:triggeredBy>
      <mailo:LegislativeAmendment rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Amend_AIAct_v1_ProhibitedPractices">
        <rdfs:label>Activation event: prohibited_practices_and_general</rdfs:label>
        <mailo:amendmentDescription>Entry into force — OJ L 2024/1689 published 12 July 2024</mailo:amendmentDescription>
        <mailo:versionStartDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2024-08-01</mailo:versionStartDate>
      </mailo:LegislativeAmendment>
    </mailo:triggeredBy>
    <mailo:versionEndDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-08-01</mailo:versionEndDate>
    <mailo:versionOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_2024_1689"/>
    <mailo:versionStartDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2024-08-01</mailo:versionStartDate>
  </mailo:RegulationVersion>
  <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#EHDS_Art68">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EHDS Art.68 — Data permit (secondary use authorisation)</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Health data access bodies issue data permits authorising secondary use of electronic health data for research, innovation and policy. Access is granted within a secure processing environment (Art.73) from which raw data cannot be downloaded; a health data request under Art.69 yields only an anonymised statistical answer. Renumbered in v5.1.0: previously recorded as Art.33, which is COM(2022) 197 proposal numbering.</rdfs:comment>
  </mailo:LegalArticle>
  <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#DataAct_Art23">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Data Act Art.23 — Switching Cloud Services</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Medical AI providers using cloud infrastructure must enable switching between cloud providers without data lock-in. Relevant for hospital AI SaaS deployment models.</rdfs:comment>
  </mailo:LegalArticle>
  <mailo:EncodingBasis rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#CourtHolding">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Court holding</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The encoded proposition is what the court decided, at the paragraphs cited.</rdfs:comment>
  </mailo:EncodingBasis>
  <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#DataAct_Art17">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Data Act Art.17 — Requests by public sector bodies for data to be made available</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The procedural requirements for a request under Chapter V: what the request must specify, and the cross-border route under Art.17(3) by which a public sector body intending to request data from a holder established in another Member State must first notify that Member State's competent authority designated under Art.37, which then examines the request against Art.17.

CORRECTED in v5.1.0: the earlier entry described Art.17 as 'B2G Data Sharing (Public Emergency)', asserting that governments may require medical AI companies to share health data in a public health emergency. Public emergency is a ground of exceptional need under Art.15, not the subject of Art.17. Art.14 states the obligation itself. The substantive claim about epidemic surveillance AI therefore rested on the wrong provision.</rdfs:comment>
  </mailo:LegalArticle>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#Patent">
    <rdfs:label>Patent</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Patent</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>A patent grant</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:Class>
  <mailo:LegalArticle rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#DGA_Art2">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">DGA Art.2 — Definitions</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines the terms used throughout the Regulation, including 'data', 'data holder', 'data user', 'data intermediation service' at Art.2(11) and 'data altruism'. CORRECTED in v5.1.0: previously labelled 'Re-use of Public Sector Health Data' and described as the Chapter II framework. Chapter II on re-use of protected public sector data runs from Art.3, with the categories at Art.3 and the conditions for re-use at Art.5.</rdfs:comment>
  </mailo:LegalArticle>
  <mailo:RegulationVersion rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_v3_OriginalHighRisk">
    <rdfs:label>Original Annex III + Annex I deadline (superseded by Omnibus provisional agreement)</rdfs:label>
    <mailo:applicablePhase>high_risk_original_deadline</mailo:applicablePhase>
    <mailo:isCurrentVersion rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">false</mailo:isCurrentVersion>
